# ATLAS matrices for the Thompson group

The two 248 by 248 binary matrices are transcribed from the ATLAS of Finite
Group Representations, representation `ThG1-f2r248B0`. Row and column labels
are shifted from 1–248 to 0–247; the entries are not transposed or inverted.
Each row is stored as a natural number whose bit `j` is column `j`.

Original MeatAxe files, provenance, SHA-256 hashes, and the transcription
script are in `Theory/SpecificGroups/Thompson/Model/source/`.
The online ATLAS is maintained by R. A. Wilson, S. J. Nickerson and J. N. Bray;
the contributor of this representation is not recorded on its page.

These are concrete matrices, with no group order or simplicity assumptions.
The small dimension of the representation makes finiteness of the eventual
matrix group immediate; its exact order and simplicity require further proofs.
